DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       If  _*_s_t_r_i_n_g_p is NULL, the ssttrrsseepp() function returns NULL and does noth‐
       ing else.  Otherwise, this function finds the first token in the string
       _*_s_t_r_i_n_g_p that is delimited by one of the bytes  in  the  string  _d_e_l_i_m.
       This  token is terminated by overwriting the delimiter with a null byte
       ('\0'), and _*_s_t_r_i_n_g_p is updated to point past the token.   In  case  no
       delimiter  was  found,  the  token  is  taken  to  be the entire string
       _*_s_t_r_i_n_g_p, and _*_s_t_r_i_n_g_p is made NULL.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       The ssttrrsseepp() function returns a pointer to the token, that is,  it  re‐
       turns the original value of _*_s_t_r_i_n_g_p.

